01:16:01.772 --> 01:16:04.081
frames per second. If we do not compress

01:16:04.081 --> 01:16:06.241
the token and fill the whole sequence into the

01:16:06.242 --> 01:16:08.432
refinement transformer, we get an

01:16:08.812 --> 01:16:11.082
acceleration, but still not real time with four

01:16:11.082 --> 01:16:13.311
frame per second. And one more

01:16:13.311 --> 01:16:15.811
t, you achieve 17 frame per second.

01:16:15.972 --> 01:16:17.982
With, the first draft of the

01:16:17.982 --> 01:16:20.062
backbone being up to 25 frame per second,

01:16:20.062 --> 01:16:22.432
but then we would have substantial reduction of quality.

01:16:24.751 --> 01:16:26.472
So in terms of what it looks like

01:16:27.032 --> 01:16:29.122
when we interact with the model, on the left, you

01:16:29.122 --> 01:16:31.282
have one, we enter an

01:16:31.282 --> 01:16:33.432
action press predict, wait a while for

01:16:33.432 --> 01:16:35.501
the few frames to be generated, On

01:16:35.502 --> 01:16:37.922
the right, we we have one more t, which instantly

01:16:37.982 --> 01:16:40.222
responds to controller actions. And

01:16:40.442 --> 01:16:42.472
you can essentially kind of play the model

01:16:42.472 --> 01:16:44.082
as you would play a game.

01:16:44.722 --> 01:16:46.921
Although it's not as fun. Well,

01:16:46.922 --> 01:16:47.712
it is quite fun.

01:16:50.432 --> 01:16:52.722
Now it's pretty good. We have a real

01:16:52.722 --> 01:16:55.002
time model that we can interact within

01:16:55.002 --> 01:16:57.082
real time, which is a great step forward in terms of

01:16:57.402 --> 01:16:59.581
being able to do prototyping. However,

01:16:59.582 --> 01:17:01.742
we still need seven years of gameplay to

01:17:01.742 --> 01:17:03.892
train one model, which is

01:17:04.132 --> 01:17:06.291
still pretty expensive. So

01:17:07.252 --> 01:17:09.592
one of the, experiments we did

01:17:09.652 --> 01:17:11.792
was first we tried to adapt one to a

01:17:11.792 --> 01:17:13.092
different type of environment.

01:17:13.862 --> 01:17:15.942
In this case, the quick two model.

01:17:16.146 --> 01:17:16.962
The quick two game.

01:17:18.402 --> 01:17:20.532
We didn't have any data from Quake two.

01:17:20.532 --> 01:17:22.242
And, again, we didn't want to crawl the web.

01:17:23.282 --> 01:17:25.621
So what we did was worked with Game Tester

01:17:25.682 --> 01:17:27.862
to collect data by giving

01:17:27.862 --> 01:17:29.942
them instructions on what we wanted to collect and how

01:17:29.942 --> 01:17:31.992
we wanted to collect the data. It

01:17:31.992 --> 01:17:33.212
was a great back and forth

01:17:34.132 --> 01:17:36.262
process where we would collect data

01:17:36.502 --> 01:17:38.622
train a model, see what the model was

01:17:38.622 --> 01:17:40.862
not doing well, and going back and collecting the missing

01:17:40.862 --> 01:17:43.040
data. By doing

01:17:43.041 --> 01:17:45.172
this data collection very intentionally, we

01:17:45.972 --> 01:17:48.072
were able to learn a full

01:17:48.072 --> 01:17:50.252
model a full level of quake

01:17:50.252 --> 01:17:52.272
two with only hundred hours of gameplay,

01:17:52.272 --> 01:17:54.452
which is a massive reduction from the

01:17:54.452 --> 01:17:56.502
seven years of gameplay that we needed.

01:17:56.976 --> 01:17:57.451
For

01:17:59.002 --> 01:18:01.142
the bleeding edge models. Some of the

01:18:01.142 --> 01:18:03.222
other learnings we got from the QUIC two

01:18:03.222 --> 01:18:05.672
model was that we this approach does generalize

01:18:05.812 --> 01:18:07.952
across games. So here I have examples

01:18:07.952 --> 01:18:10.201
of two of two games, but we did try

01:18:10.202 --> 01:18:11.352
a few games internally.

01:18:12.952 --> 01:18:15.191
And we also managed to double the resolution

01:18:15.192 --> 01:18:17.652
at no additional inference cost by simply improving

01:18:17.652 --> 01:18:19.652
our tokenizer slightly. You

01:18:19.712 --> 01:18:22.052
wanna play the quick model, it is available on Copilot

01:18:22.112 --> 01:18:24.342
Labs. Just for the

01:18:24.342 --> 01:18:24.842
QR code.

